title: अव्ययीभावसमासः

 अव्ययीभावसमासः  

You will recognize the अव्ययीभावसमासः   in words

* Where the first part of the word is an अव्यय or a निपात  
>,,(निपाताः  are particles which possess no gender and number and the case termination after which is dropped or elided. For example चादयः (च  and others) and प्रादयः (प्र and others),,
* The second part of the word is a noun (सञ्ज्ञा).
* The combined word is an @@color:yellow;अव्यय and is नपुं. एकवचनम् |@@
* The combined word समस्तपदम्   is different from the विग्रहः , because the अव्यय conveys a  special meaning to the noun.
* in the above table we have listeb the avyayas followed by the samastapada to which the avaya is attached as a prefix and the vigraha which is the explanation of or breaking the samastapada

